BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fluxus-cpga-prize-frieze-london-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260926T162454Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260928
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260929
SUMMARY:Deadline: Fluxus-CPGA Prize at Frieze London 2026
DESCRIPTION:The Fluxus-CPGA Prize at Frieze London\, a collaboration betwee
 n Fluxus Art Projects\, the Comite Professionnel des Galeries d'Art and Fr
 ieze London\, supports talent from the French art scene and promotes its v
 isibility internationally. It also celebrates the relationship between art
 ists and their galleries: the GBP 15\,000 prize is shared between the two.
  WHO APPLIES: galleries of any nationality exhibiting at Frieze London 202
 6\, presenting the work of one French or French-based artist on their stan
 d\; artists cannot apply directly. HOW TO APPLY: via the Google Form linke
 d from the apply page\, with gallery contact information\, the artist's na
 me and number of works presented\, an artist biography (200 words)\, a gal
 lery description (200 words) and 1 to 2 images. Free of charge. Previous l
 aureates include Daiga Grantina (Emalin\, 2025)\, Stephanie Saade (Marfa' 
 Projects\, 2024) and Josefa Ntjam (Nicoletti\, 2023)\; jurors have include
 d Hans Ulrich Obrist\, Zoe Whitley\, Catherine Wood and Valeria Napoleone.
  Deadline 28 September 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Fluxus Art Projects\, with t
 he Comite Professionnel des Galeries d'Art and Frieze London\nLocation: Fr
 ieze London\, Regent's Park\, London\, UK (October 2026). Galleries of any
  nationality can apply\, provided they present the work of a French or Fre
 nch-based artist on their stand.\nAward: GBP 15\,000 prize\, shared betwee
 n the artist and their gallery. Participation is free of charge.\nDuration
 : Awarded during Frieze London in October 2026\n\nMore: https://fluxusartp
 rojects.com/apply?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referra
 l
URL:https://fluxusartprojects.com/apply?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Frieze London\, Regent's Park\, London\, UK (October 2026). Galler
 ies of any nationality can apply\, provided they present the work of a Fre
 nch or French-based artist on their stand.
END:VEVENT
